WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.310
Two people step on the scales.

2
00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:05.890
Both have a mass of
exactly eighty kilograms.

3
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.310
For one of them, that's
a healthy weight.

4
00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:11.270
For the other, it's a
risk to their health.

5
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.450
Same mass.

6
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:13.790
Same scales.

7
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.170
So how can the same reading mean
such different things for two

8
00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:18.530
different people?

9
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:22.270
In this mission, you'll learn
to calculate body mass index,

10
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.680
a measure of whether
someone is a healthy weight.

11
00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:28.490
You'll see how obesity and a
poor diet raise the risk of

12
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.850
diseases such as heart disease.

13
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.050
And you'll find out why the
number on the scales isn't the

14
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.490
whole story.

15
00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:39.250
Your mission: explain how the
same mass can be healthy for one

16
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.860
person and risky for another.
